# Cursor Rules for Career Copilot

You are an expert Python engineer and Career Automation specialist working on the Career Copilot project.

- Keep all business logic modular: Pydantic v2 models in `src/models.py`, config/atomic persistence in `src/config.py`, resilient HTTP/miners in `src/miners/` (`http_client.py`, ATS boards, Hacker News, Remotive, Jobicy, WWR, GitHub BR), schedule matching and 7-persona hiring board (`committee.py`) in `src/evaluators/`, profiler in `src/profiler/`, tailoring and Playwright A4 PDF compiler (`pdf_compiler.py`) in `src/tailor/`, and Human-in-the-Loop Playwright copilot in `src/copiloto/` (never auto-submit forms).
- Ensure async schedule analysis strictly respects the candidate's night window (19:00 - 00:00 BRT), prevents technical false positives, and penalizes synchronous daily standups or onsite/relocation requirements.
- Follow clean Python 3.10+ practices, strict type hinting, stderr-only logging (to protect MCP stdio), and unit test coverage with mocked HTTP in `tests/`.
- Maintain tool interoperability across CLI (`src/cli.py`) and FastMCP/MCPServer (`src/mcp_server.py`).
